  "activity": {
    "id": "vsepr_activity",
    "name": "VSEPR Theory: Predicting Molecular Geometry",
    "description": "A progressive AR lab guiding students from Lewis structures through the VSEPR minimum-repulsion principle, the five electron-domain geometries, the distinction between electron-domain and molecular geometry, lone pair angular asymmetry, real molecule examples, and two interactive prediction challenges, ending with a recap.",
    "language": "en",
    "workplace": "vsepr_workplace",
    "start": "step1_intro",
    "actions": [
      {
        "id": "step1_intro",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "hololens1",
        "location": "central_workspace",
        "predicate": "narration_intro",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "Introduction to VSEPR Theory",
          "description": "A central atom appears before you. Electrons in bonding pairs and lone pairs repel each other, so the molecule adopts whatever 3D shape places these electron domains as far apart as possible. Review the sample Lewis structure of water on the reference panel \u2014 count each single bond, double bond, triple bond, or lone pair as one electron domain. Click Start when ready."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "central_atom_model",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "narration_intro",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "central_atom_model",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "label_molecule_name",
              "poi": "label_point",
              "text": "Central Atom (A)"
            },
            {
              "target": "lewis_structure_water",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "img_lewis_water",
              "poi": "default"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "lewis_structure_water",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "start",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          },
          {
            "mode": "voice",
            "id": "start",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "step2_repulsion_principle",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "hololens1",
        "location": "central_workspace",
        "predicate": "narration_repulsion",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "Minimum-Repulsion Principle",
          "description": "Watch two electron domain clouds drift apart until they settle 180\u00b0 apart (linear). Then a third domain is added and the set rearranges into a trigonal planar shape at 120\u00b0. A fourth domain produces a tetrahedron at 109.5\u00b0. Faint repulsion vectors appear during each rearrangement and fade once stable. Say 'next' when you understand the pattern."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "electron_domain_set",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "anim_domain_repulsion",
              "poi": "domain_slot_1"
            },
            {
              "target": "electron_domain_set",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "narration_repulsion",
              "poi": "domain_slot_1"
            },
            {
              "target": "electron_domain_set",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "label_domain_count",
              "poi": "domain_slot_2",
              "text": "Domains: 2 \u2192 3 \u2192 4"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "electron_domain_set",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "voice",
            "id": "next",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          },
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "next",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "step3_five_geometries",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "hololens1",
        "location": "central_workspace",
        "predicate": "narration_five_geometries",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "The Five Electron-Domain Geometries",
          "description": "Building from the tetrahedron, a fifth domain produces trigonal bipyramidal geometry (3 equatorial at 120\u00b0, 2 axial at 90\u00b0). A sixth domain produces octahedral geometry (all neighbors at 90\u00b0). Rotate the molecule freely to inspect it from any angle. The summary panel shows all five geometries with domain counts (2,3,4,5,6) and angles (180\u00b0,120\u00b0,109.5\u00b0,90\u00b0/120\u00b0,90\u00b0). Detect the panel marker to continue."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "electron_domain_set",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "anim_tbp_octahedral",
              "poi": "domain_slot_1"
            },
            {
              "target": "electron_domain_set",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "narration_five_geometries",
              "poi": "domain_slot_1"
            },
            {
              "target": "reference_panel_zone",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "img_summary_geometries",
              "poi": "panel_face"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "electron_domain_set",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            },
            {
              "target": "reference_panel_zone",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            }
          ],
