          "description": "Methane, ammonia, and water are displayed side by side with bond angles labeled: 109.5\u00b0, 107\u00b0, and 104.5\u00b0. Notice that lone-pair clouds render larger than bonding domains \u2014 lone pairs are held only by the central atom, so they spread out more and compress the bonding angles. Toggle the overlay to directly compare how the H-X-H angle decreases as lone pairs are added. Click to proceed."
